        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12388430/comment/12573742",
          "id": "12573742",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=olegk",
            "name": "olegk",
            "key": "olegk",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Oleg Kalnichevski",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Berlin"
          },
          "body": "Stojce,\n\nWould you mind using maps of objects (Map<String, Object>) instead of maps of lists of strings (Map<String, List<String>>)? In my opinion this would make the API somewhat less cumbersome, especially for simple cases. If an object is an instance of Collection, you could still treat it as such, whereas non-collection objects would be simply converted to their textual representation with Object#toString? Could you live with that?\n\nCould please also update the ClientFormLogin sample?\n\nOleg",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=olegk",
            "name": "olegk",
            "key": "olegk",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Oleg Kalnichevski",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Berlin"
          },
          "created": "2008-02-29T13:45:25.384+0000",
          "updated": "2008-02-29T13:45:25.384+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12388430/comment/12573803",
          "id": "12573803",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=sdmiski",
            "name": "sdmiski",
            "key": "sdmiski",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Stojce Dimski",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "body": "I understand your concerns regarding the user-friendly api, but I insist that 'Map<String, List<String>>' is crystal clear and more consistent/explicit, also implementation is more simple. For easier use we can make some static utility methods...",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=sdmiski",
            "name": "sdmiski",
            "key": "sdmiski",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Stojce Dimski",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "created": "2008-02-29T16:02:00.416+0000",
          "updated": "2008-02-29T16:02:00.416+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12388430/comment/12573862",
          "id": "12573862",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=olegk",
            "name": "olegk",
            "key": "olegk",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Oleg Kalnichevski",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Berlin"
          },
          "body": "Could you then please keep the original UrlEncodedFormEntity(final NameValuePair[] fields) constructor for people like me?\n\nOleg",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=olegk",
            "name": "olegk",
            "key": "olegk",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
